{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1567545158,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0ODg4Mjc0ODM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3650","origin":"github"},"title":"Some commands confusingly have both relative path semantics","message":"When looking into another issue, I noticed that install() when called as a dataset method was fine with both a path relative to the dataset (as expected) and a path relative to the current working directory.  See the script below for an example.  I haven't tested to see what happens when the two rules collide (i.e. different paths exist for each rule).\n\nI say \"some commands\" in the title because a quick glance suggests that the handling in install() is probably coming from a get() call.\n\nThis happens on both 0.11.x and master.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003escript\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport tempfile\n\nimport datalad.api as dl\nfrom datalad.utils import chpwd\n\ntdir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"dl-\"))\n\n# Set up source.\n\nsource_path = tdir / \"source\"\nsource = dl.Dataset(str(source_path)).create()\n(source_path / \"subdir\").mkdir()\n(source_path / \"subdir\" / \"foo\").write_text(\"foo\")\nsource.create(\"subds\")\nsource.add([\"subds\", \"subdir\"])\n\n# Clone.\n\nclone_path = tdir / \"clone\"\ndl.clone(source=source, path=str(clone_path))\nclone = dl.Dataset(str(clone_path))\n\n# As expected, when called from subdirectory, calling install() as a\n# dataset method with path relative to dataset works.\n\nassert not (clone_path / \"subds\" / \".gitattributes\").exists()\nwith chpwd(str(clone_path / \"subdir\")):\n    clone.install(\"subds\")\nassert (clone_path / \"subds\" / \".gitattributes\").exists()\n\n# Confusingly, giving a path relative to PWD also works.\n\nclone.uninstall(\"subds\")\nassert not (clone_path / \"subds\" / \".gitattributes\").exists()\nwith chpwd(str(clone_path / \"subdir\")):\n    clone.install(\"../subds\")\nassert (clone_path / \"subds\" / \".gitattributes\").exists()\n```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e","files":null}]}